1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,275
The Rise of Game Subscription Services.

2
00:00:03,225 --> 00:00:15,637
Game subscription services have cemented themselves as the dominant distribution model in 2026, with PlayStation Plus and Xbox Game Pass collectively reaching over 100 million subscribers worldwide.

3
00:00:15,637 --> 00:00:25,937
Microsoft's Game Pass continues to lead the market, offering day-one access to first-party titles including the blockbuster Fable reboot and the latest Forza Motorsport entry.

4
00:00:25,937 --> 00:00:35,600
Sony's revamped PlayStation Plus, now structured in three tiers, has grown steadily by leaning on its back catalog of exclusives and third-party partnerships.

5
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:43,987
Subscriptions now account for roughly 35 percent of the total gaming market revenue, up from below 20 percent in 2022.

6
00:00:43,987 --> 00:00:51,225
Critics argue that the model raises concerns about game ownership, as titles can be removed from services at any time.

7
00:00:51,225 --> 00:01:00,837
Nonetheless, publishers increasingly view subscriptions as a reliable revenue stream, with Ubisoft and Electronic Arts also expanding their own services.

8
00:01:00,837 --> 00:01:04,075
The model shows no signs of slowing down.

